WEBVTT

00:09.676 --> 00:12.762
It has finally arrived!

00:16.474 --> 00:17.892
It looks like it's starting.

00:18.935 --> 00:21.271
This science showdown…

00:40.081 --> 00:43.126
I'll show you what
a professional flight looks like.

00:43.793 --> 00:46.880
This is the final battle to avenge Senku!

00:48.423 --> 00:50.341
I'm still alive, though.

01:01.352 --> 01:03.438
It's a science-versus-science…

01:04.522 --> 01:06.191
dogfight!

01:19.329 --> 01:21.998
Time to fight! Stanley!

01:22.999 --> 01:28.505
&lrm;ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
&lrm;SHUEISHA JUMP COMICS

03:15.111 --> 03:17.780
A dogfight! An airplane showdown!

03:17.864 --> 03:20.533
This isn't the time to get all excited.

03:20.617 --> 03:23.995
We have to win,
or he'll shoot us down from above!

03:24.078 --> 03:25.830
That's true!

03:25.914 --> 03:28.166
But why is Senku on the plane?

03:28.249 --> 03:30.168
He hasn't recovered yet!

03:41.012 --> 03:43.473
Wait, is Senku holding a machine gun?

03:43.556 --> 03:46.726
-But when did he…
-That's not it.

03:46.809 --> 03:51.189
The only gun
is the one Ryusui took from me.

03:54.400 --> 03:56.778
What's that? Just a regular stick?

03:56.861 --> 04:00.281
Yes, if he found out
we don't have machine guns,

04:00.365 --> 04:03.493
he’d just get close and gun us down.
We’d be done for.

04:04.953 --> 04:05.995
I see!

04:06.079 --> 04:08.289
If we show off some fake fangs,

04:08.373 --> 04:11.334
we can turn this into a real dogfight!

04:13.628 --> 04:15.797
You've got some guts,

04:15.880 --> 04:17.840
challenging a military fighter pilot.

04:17.924 --> 04:19.592
Well, as you wish.

04:19.676 --> 04:21.928
I'll crush you fair and square!

04:37.777 --> 04:40.947
Senku's plane and… Stanley's?

04:41.030 --> 04:43.574
They're going in circles,
chasing each other!

04:44.659 --> 04:47.745
A battle between fighter jets
is about locking onto the enemy

04:47.829 --> 04:49.455
with precise gunfire.

04:50.039 --> 04:53.001
The one who gets on the enemy's tail wins!

04:53.084 --> 04:57.505
Therefore, they keep chasing
and circling each other.

04:57.588 --> 04:59.215
You're so talkative all of a sudden!

05:01.175 --> 05:04.554
It's because I draw military manga!

05:08.099 --> 05:10.518
This is damn heavy.

05:10.601 --> 05:13.938
It's like a double-spin
roller coaster ride.

05:14.022 --> 05:15.732
The G-force is insane!

05:17.692 --> 05:19.527
Something went off!

05:20.570 --> 05:22.405
It's a rushed job, after all.

05:22.488 --> 05:25.450
No problem,
this is why I'm on this plane too!

05:32.206 --> 05:34.334
He's tailing us!

05:36.169 --> 05:40.089
Because we only ever fly
the private plane for everyday errands.

05:40.173 --> 05:42.216
No, we don't.

05:43.092 --> 05:45.636
The enemy is an elite
military fighter pilot.

05:45.720 --> 05:47.805
In an all-out speed battle,

05:47.889 --> 05:50.975
we're bound to lose in the end.

05:51.684 --> 05:53.686
Stanley is way faster than me.

05:54.353 --> 05:55.855
We'll take advantage of that!

06:02.737 --> 06:06.074
A break turn! He's so good!

06:06.157 --> 06:07.909
In the sky, there's no emergency brake!

06:07.992 --> 06:10.286
<i>Especially in a primitive airplane!</i>

06:10.369 --> 06:13.456
<i>If they make Stanley overshoot,</i>
<i>or in other words, pass them,</i>

06:13.539 --> 06:16.250
they will turn the tables!

06:16.334 --> 06:17.627
They can get on his tail

06:17.710 --> 06:20.088
and lock onto him!

06:29.931 --> 06:31.390
We've got your six!

06:38.606 --> 06:41.692
<i>Stanley just… disappeared…</i>

06:48.491 --> 06:51.327
Hey, science club.

06:51.410 --> 06:53.788
Is this your first time seeing this?

06:58.167 --> 06:59.418
Is that…

07:00.294 --> 07:02.839
<i>By rapidly going up,</i>
<i>he'll make a sharp deceleration</i>

07:02.922 --> 07:05.633
<i>to force his way into his opponent's turn.</i>

07:05.716 --> 07:08.553
<i>Then he'll aggressively</i>
<i>dive and accelerate,</i>

07:08.636 --> 07:10.972
<i>quickly catching up and taking their tail!</i>

07:12.598 --> 07:14.767
<i>Like the movement of a yo-yo…</i>

07:16.269 --> 07:20.690
<i>it's an attack technique</i>
<i>known as the high-speed yo-yo!</i>

07:21.274 --> 07:24.152
Damn, he's too good.

07:24.235 --> 07:27.530
Even with this primitive airplane…

07:28.030 --> 07:29.532
I want it.

07:29.615 --> 07:31.033
Stanley…

07:31.617 --> 07:33.911
Skills like that bastard's…

07:34.495 --> 07:35.663
His abilities!

07:42.462 --> 07:44.464
He's on their tail again!

07:44.547 --> 07:47.842
This is bad!
They're in the range to be shot down.

07:48.968 --> 07:53.431
A dogfight is like a 3D chess game,

07:53.514 --> 07:58.060
constantly trading speed, altitude,
and energy at hyper speeds.

07:58.936 --> 08:01.731
Amateurs have no chance to win.

08:04.692 --> 08:06.360
Locked on.

08:08.070 --> 08:09.530
It's over.

08:09.614 --> 08:12.700
Excuse me for ending your lives,
science club.

08:12.783 --> 08:16.037
Wait for me in hell.

08:17.705 --> 08:19.916
Thank you, Stanley!

08:19.999 --> 08:22.043
If it weren't
for this desperate situation,

08:22.126 --> 08:26.547
I would never attempt such
a life-threatening aerial maneuver!

08:29.717 --> 08:33.346
I want to master
his awesome techniques and abilities!

08:35.056 --> 08:36.057
<i>Seriously?</i>

08:46.317 --> 08:49.028
They're suddenly pulling up vertically!

08:50.488 --> 08:54.408
<i>A Cobra maneuver? No way he can</i>
<i>pull that off on that primitive airplane!</i>

08:54.492 --> 08:56.827
<i>They will stall and crash!</i>

08:56.911 --> 08:59.497
I know the power of that engine.

08:59.580 --> 09:02.833
There's no way it has enough power
to recover its position!

09:12.510 --> 09:13.344
&lrm;How did they do it?

09:15.930 --> 09:18.849
I'm ten billion percent sure
it doesn't have enough power.

09:18.933 --> 09:22.478
Your fuel alone won’t be enough!

09:23.688 --> 09:27.733
…and finally, some castor beans…

09:28.401 --> 09:32.738
<i>Castor oil is a superior kind</i>
<i>of motor oil.</i>

09:33.698 --> 09:38.119
<i>We don't have oil flowing out</i>
<i>like the American continent, you know.</i>

09:38.202 --> 09:42.039
<i>This is the product</i>
<i>of poor Japan's desperate measures!</i>

09:53.926 --> 09:56.679
My right hand, trained through gaming,

09:56.762 --> 10:00.516
and your science tag-team technique,
Senku.

10:02.143 --> 10:04.270
A complete turnaround!

10:08.399 --> 10:10.943
Hey, Stanley.

10:11.027 --> 10:12.820
It's our turn now.

10:13.654 --> 10:15.239
Locked on!

10:31.839 --> 10:33.841
He's jinking?

10:33.924 --> 10:34.967
What does that mean?

10:35.051 --> 10:38.429
Stanley is intentionally
shaking the aircraft!

10:40.222 --> 10:42.683
<i>I can't hit him like this.</i>

10:43.643 --> 10:44.644
You can do it!

10:45.269 --> 10:48.189
Come on, Senku and Ryusui!

10:48.898 --> 10:51.901
<i>I'll just cheer you up</i>
<i>from this safe spot.</i>

10:53.736 --> 10:56.572
If they shoot him down,
the sky will be ours!

10:56.656 --> 10:58.741
But if they couldn't take him down,

10:58.824 --> 11:01.035
the next ones to be
riddled with bullets are us!

11:01.118 --> 11:02.745
What?

11:02.828 --> 11:05.206
Try harder, you two!

11:05.790 --> 11:08.626
-Come on!
-Come on!

11:08.709 --> 11:09.752
You got this!

11:10.503 --> 11:12.046
<i>What a flashy air combat.</i>

11:12.546 --> 11:15.174
<i>It’s drawn everyone’s attention</i>
<i>to the sky.</i>

11:15.925 --> 11:17.968
<i>That's why someone has to keep a lookout</i>

11:18.552 --> 11:19.512
<i>down here.</i>

11:24.100 --> 11:26.060
<i>That's why down there,</i>

11:26.644 --> 11:31.273
<i>there could be some vigilant</i>
<i>boys and girls keeping a lookout.</i>

11:32.274 --> 11:35.236
<i>But too bad for them.</i>

11:35.736 --> 11:40.241
<i>Because I am one step ahead of that.</i>

11:47.832 --> 11:50.251
<i>I'm going to show them</i>

11:51.043 --> 11:53.129
<i>the elegant,</i>

11:53.921 --> 11:56.924
<i>world of 21st-century</i>

11:58.509 --> 12:01.011
<i>human science.</i>

12:08.519 --> 12:11.647
-You got this!
-You got this!

12:11.730 --> 12:14.024
-Go get him!
-Go get him!

12:14.692 --> 12:15.985
-Come on!
-Come on!

12:20.364 --> 12:21.949
What the…?

12:22.032 --> 12:24.118
What…?

12:26.036 --> 12:28.831
A submarine?

12:28.914 --> 12:29.915
No way!

13:02.031 --> 13:04.783
Hands on your head!

13:04.867 --> 13:06.243
Get down on the floor, kids!

13:06.327 --> 13:09.038
Anyone who moves will be shot on the spot!

13:09.121 --> 13:10.581
Eh?

13:22.051 --> 13:24.011
-Clear!
-Clear!

13:25.763 --> 13:27.681
Hey, Luna.

13:31.018 --> 13:33.521
They took me ten seconds.

13:35.731 --> 13:38.651
-Can I sing?
-Please, don't…

13:42.738 --> 13:45.824
Looks like the kids'
main stronghold has fallen.

13:46.492 --> 13:51.288
Did they really attack them
using the submarine?

13:51.997 --> 13:54.291
Science versus science.

13:55.042 --> 13:58.462
It's a chess game for control
over the New World's leadership.

14:01.382 --> 14:03.592
It's a complete victory for us.

14:04.385 --> 14:08.847
The battle for air supremacy
isn't just fought in the skies.

14:09.890 --> 14:11.058
I'm sorry.

14:11.141 --> 14:13.811
Once we take over
the aircraft carrier's runway,

14:13.894 --> 14:16.855
which is the only place
your friends on the plane can land,

14:16.939 --> 14:18.732
victory will be ours.

14:25.781 --> 14:28.200
He's doing such an impressive
jinking maneuver.

14:28.826 --> 14:32.121
It's not himself doing it,
but that we made him do it.

14:32.204 --> 14:35.165
This is exactly why we made it
look like we had a machine gun.

14:35.791 --> 14:37.918
This is a battle of wits.

14:38.002 --> 14:41.672
Stanley converted his speed
into turbulence.

14:41.755 --> 14:45.259
This means that, right at this moment,

14:45.342 --> 14:48.178
I'm ten billion percent sure
he's getting slower.

14:50.514 --> 14:51.515
I see!

14:55.060 --> 14:57.855
<i>Senku and Ryusui are suddenly pulling up.</i>

14:57.938 --> 14:59.481
<i>But why?</i>

15:00.316 --> 15:02.776
Normally, speed decreases
when you pull up.

15:03.402 --> 15:06.155
But Stanley did us a favor
by slowing down.

15:06.238 --> 15:07.907
So now's the perfect moment

15:08.490 --> 15:10.409
to take the high ground!

15:12.244 --> 15:13.662
<i>What are they doing?</i>

15:14.371 --> 15:16.916
<i>They had already tailed me and locked on.</i>

15:16.999 --> 15:18.500
<i>Why are they pulling up?</i>

15:19.251 --> 15:20.419
<i>No way!</i>

15:22.129 --> 15:24.924
Yep, there's no way.

15:25.007 --> 15:28.636
At least not
with the Old World rules, Stanley.

15:29.470 --> 15:30.304
But…

15:31.138 --> 15:35.142
In this New World,
we have to make our own rules!

15:35.225 --> 15:38.520
The first-ever dogfights in human history

15:38.604 --> 15:42.191
were ridiculously primitive,
they just threw things at each other.

15:43.484 --> 15:46.153
We're just a little bit more than that.

15:46.236 --> 15:48.489
Isn't this a battle of wits?

15:49.490 --> 15:53.243
Acetylene gas is an engine’s worst enemy!

15:54.244 --> 15:58.082
<i>If it gets into the engine,</i>
<i>it will ten billion percent make it stop.</i>

16:01.627 --> 16:04.922
Take this with gratitude!

16:05.005 --> 16:07.174
A carpet bombing

16:07.257 --> 16:08.842
of handmade acetylene gas!

16:12.137 --> 16:15.891
You knew too many old rules, Stanley.

16:33.033 --> 16:34.702
There's more of them inside the ship!

16:36.787 --> 16:39.123
What was it again? A machine gun?

16:39.206 --> 16:42.209
Are those the best
melee weapons you've got?

16:42.292 --> 16:46.463
You thought everyone would be
shaking in fear and surrender

16:46.547 --> 16:48.924
the moment you showed them that,
didn't you?

16:53.804 --> 16:57.099
I wonder if our island warrior tag team
will go down that easily.

16:57.182 --> 16:59.560
Who knows, anyway?

17:05.024 --> 17:08.360
What are you doing here?
Why aren't you in your position?

17:09.028 --> 17:10.863
It's not possible…

17:10.946 --> 17:15.868
Aren't they afraid of facing a machine gun
with just swords and spears?

17:16.535 --> 17:17.828
Those…

17:23.959 --> 17:26.211
This pipe spear is good!

17:27.838 --> 17:29.798
The reach is different.

17:42.144 --> 17:45.981
This is the first time in my life
I've ever had a special training.

17:46.774 --> 17:48.942
Everyone, meet up
from the top of the stairs!

17:54.531 --> 17:55.783
Hand grenades!

17:59.411 --> 18:02.456
<i>A wide-range attack,</i>
<i>just like the petrification device…</i>

18:03.123 --> 18:06.168
<i>The counterattack</i>
<i>for that abominable weapon…</i>

18:07.002 --> 18:09.296
<i>Like that time a few centuries ago…</i>

18:09.379 --> 18:12.174
<i>Let's see how much I've improved.</i>

18:19.973 --> 18:24.853
It's good how your old
and new abilities match.

18:24.937 --> 18:27.856
-Damn!
-Don't do that!

18:27.940 --> 18:30.567
You could get a lot of us killed
in a narrow space like this.

18:32.319 --> 18:36.115
Even the kids would get caught up and die.

18:36.198 --> 18:39.451
You might want living slaves
because you're short on manpower.

18:39.535 --> 18:41.578
So let's not act recklessly.

18:42.162 --> 18:45.249
Right? We can afford to take them, though…

18:47.793 --> 18:50.212
That's dirty…

18:50.295 --> 18:53.382
Apart from being selfish
and insanely strong, he's so calculating!

18:54.007 --> 18:56.009
He's the worst as an enemy,

18:56.093 --> 18:58.971
but quite reassuring as an ally…

18:59.054 --> 19:02.975
Hey, no one's acting recklessly. Look!

19:03.058 --> 19:06.436
It looks like the dogfight is over.

19:09.064 --> 19:10.607
Well…

19:11.108 --> 19:15.445
We got the acetylene gas
into the enemy's engine…

19:17.865 --> 19:20.325
We shot Stanley down!

19:34.131 --> 19:35.966
<i>Could that be…?</i>

19:37.384 --> 19:40.053
<i>Yes, it got into our engine too.</i>

20:04.077 --> 20:05.871
Senku, can you walk?

20:05.954 --> 20:07.748
It doesn't matter…

20:11.627 --> 20:12.753
There's the enemy's plane.

20:13.378 --> 20:14.880
Let's secure…

20:16.673 --> 20:19.134
<i>Did Stanley dodge at this distance?</i>

20:32.272 --> 20:33.899
Who the heck are you?

20:34.691 --> 20:37.444
You're not Stanley Snyder.

20:38.362 --> 20:39.738
Exactly!

20:39.821 --> 20:42.032
If I were the real Captain Stanley,

20:42.115 --> 20:43.909
I wouldn't have dodged.

20:43.992 --> 20:47.204
He would have eliminated you in one shot!

20:47.871 --> 20:50.332
If the god-tier sniper were keeping watch,

20:50.415 --> 20:52.709
you would have stayed inside the ship.

20:53.752 --> 20:56.755
In that case, taking over
wouldn’t have been a real struggle.

21:02.010 --> 21:06.807
Well, since it's over,
this hide-and-seek is over too.

21:06.890 --> 21:08.684
Here comes the main character.

21:30.080 --> 21:32.499
We caught them all.

21:33.208 --> 21:36.420
Mission accomplished.

21:38.880 --> 21:40.549
Delivering checkmate

21:40.632 --> 21:43.802
with the strongest knight
is truly elegant.

21:45.554 --> 21:48.557
It's a checkmate, no doubt.

21:51.393 --> 21:53.061
Yes, a checkmate…

21:54.271 --> 21:56.148
<i>delivered with the strongest knight!</i>

22:08.035 --> 22:10.162
This works both ways…

23:53.056 --> 23:55.851
NEXT EPISODE

23:55.934 --> 23:58.687
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:58.770 --> 24:00.856
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM MAY BE
DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL, SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:00.939 --> 24:01.815
Subtitle translation by: Silvia
